":"2026-11-01T19:12:07Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/download/v0.1.12/prism-inference-0.1.12-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.receipt.json"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/assets/699259524","id":699259524,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVWipD84prdqE","name":"prism-inference-0.1.12-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"symbiogenesis","id":1724472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ0NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis","html_url":"https://github.com/symbiogenesis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":3471826,"digest":"sha256:a1c505792deae7765fcc9f96dd27d7db37611b17da767fbf8a2244c372d2d553","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-11-01T19:12:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T19:12:08Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/download/v0.1.12/prism-inference-0.1.12-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/tarball/v0.1.12","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/zipball/v0.1.12","body":"# Prism Inference 0.1.12\r\n\r\nThis full release rolls up the improvements since the last full release,\r\n`v0.1.6` (`02c8a24b31ac1c35f2ffd3530f6a753ce440bdc0`). It supplies the Rust library,\r\nsource tools and prebuilt Windows ARM64/x64 CPU bundles. A full release does not\r\nmake the experimental model profiles or accelerators qualified defaults.\r\n\r\n## Improvements since 0.1.6\r\n\r\n| Area | Result |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Contained startup | Exact read paths are checked inside AppContainer without requiring broader directory access; bounded startup-stage diagnostics retain no artifact paths or values. |\r\n| Model profiles | The Swift session and private HTTP service can explicitly select the verified current-weight PTQ1 export and approved rank-one adapter. Adapter scales are bounded and bound to prepared requests; changing a scale clears incompatible live state and checkpoints. |\r\n| CPU workers | The optional `parallel-rows` feature provides a persistent, explicitly budgeted packed-row pool. Private readiness reports the instantiated session's effective worker budget, allowing the owner to reject a policy mismatch. |\r\n| Artifact verification | GGUF verification uses Windows CNG SHA-256 with a portable Rust implementation elsewhere. Exact file length, digest and the retained read-only handle remain mandatory; existing payload-loading progress/cancellation behavior is unchanged. |\r\n| State reuse | Library callers can explicitly select `PromptReuse::Latest`; ownership, exact-prefix and adapter-scale checks prevent incompatible reuse. The private service resets for every request by default; latest-prefix reuse requires explicit selection. |\r\n| Correctness and delivery | Added regressions cover row-worker parity and failure recovery, sampled and hybrid-state reuse, adapter profile boundaries and hash streams. Source-only rollback and private-service capture tools support further bounded qualification. |\r\n| Rust consumers | GGUF now has its own `0.1.1` source identity and the runtime pins it exactly. Hosted source-package checks exercise packaged dependencies and an external library consumer. Installation and library examples distinguish GitHub source/binaries from registry publication. |\r\n\r\nThe production recurrent update retains the prior copy-then-scale arithmetic.\r\nThe proposed fused copy/decay implementation is test-only pending its own\r\nqualification. This release claims no measured startup, throughput or memory gain.\r\n\r\n## Supported release scope\r\n\r\nThe first generation path remains the pinned Swift/Bonsai dense Qwen35 CPU\r\narchitecture. Original PQ2, one row worker, no adapter and fresh private-service\r\nrequest state remain the defaults. The runtime has no C/C++ inference dependency;\r\nthe existing Rust import path remains `bonsai_prism_runtime`.\r\n\r\nPTQ1, approved-adapter execution, extra row workers and exact-prefix reuse require\r\nexplicit selection. Their device, numerical, quality and resource qualification\r\nremains scoped to the exact evidence already documented in the\r\n[roadmap](roadmap.md), [worker contract](parallel-rows.md),\r\n[adapter contract](rank-one-adapter.md) and\r\n[profile contract](swift-session-profiles.md). Full-context trajectories, adapter\r\nauthoring provenance, sustained comfort, application isolation and installation\r\nacceptance remain open. These limits also prevent automatic promotion in Runner.\r\n\r\nThe isolated, unpublished native Hexagon diagnostic crate is outside the five\r\nbundled CPU executables. It enables no model offload or accelerator profile.\r\nBroader model architectures and general model selection remain future work.\r\n\r\n## Installation and provenance\r\n\r\nUse the versioned Windows archives and matching integrity receipts attached to\r\nthe release, or the pinned Git source instructions in the\r\n[build guide](build-and-validation.md). Models and adapters are separate artifacts.\r\nEach binary receipt records its source revision, compiler, target, complete file\r\ninventory and archive/file SHA-256 digests. Older releases remain available for\r\nrollback; this release does not repin an application's existing runtime lock.\r\n\r\nThe release requires successful Foundation, runtime conformance and source-package\r\nchecks on its exact source revision. Binary attachments must be the unchanged\r\nFoundation artifacts for that revision. The published release notes retain links\r\nto those successful owning runs.\r\n\r\nRegistry publication is a separate delivery channel: publish `bonsai-native-hash`\r\n`0.1.0`, then `bonsai-gguf` `0.1.1`, then `prism-inference` `0.1.12`. Source-package\r\nchecks exercise these packages before publication; they do not publish them.\r\nThe private server retains its exact Git credential-helper dependency and is not\r\nregistry-published. Use the documented Git source dependency until the matching\r\nregistry versions are available.\r\n\n## Validation for this release\n\nSource: `c48687616f55eec9aff0de04860917de3e1047f2` on `main`.\n\n- [Foundation](https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/actions/runs/41337320095): native Windows ARM64/x64 correctness, analyzers, feature variants and binary bundles, plus Linux native storage overlay.\n- [Runtime conformance](https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/actions/runs/41337320096): owning upstream source/backend and native codec gates.\n- [Source package](https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/actions/runs/41337320097): verified normalized Cargo archives and independent scalar/default/parallel Rust consumers on Windows ARM64, Windows x64 and Linux ARM64.\n\nThe attached archives and receipts are the unchanged Foundation artifacts for\nthis source. Their archive digests, complete nine-file inventories, individual\nfile digests and executable targets were verified before publication. All three\nowning workflows passed at the source above. No new owner-device model trial,\nbenchmark result or automatic application/default promotion is claimed.\n## Rust API migration from 0.1.6\n\n`MatvecStatistics` adds the public `parallel_row_operations` counter. Callers\nusing `Default` or reading existing fields need no change. Update exhaustive\nstruct literals to supply the new field (or use `..Default::default()`), and\nuse `..` when destructuring only selected fields. Existing public methods and\nexports remain available; this release retains the established prerelease API."},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/430764784","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/430764784/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/430764784/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/symbiogenesis/prism-inference/releases/tag/v0.1.11","id":430764784,"author":{"login":"symbiogenesis","id":1724472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ0NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis","html_url":"https://github.com/symbiogenesis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/symbiogenesis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOVWipD84ZrPLw","tag_name":"v0.1.11","target_commitish":"4ce85bdd92f30dc4badb4b5f16307611fa6408c7","name":"Pris